---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="KL Divergence — Made Visual" description="An interactive visual guide to KL divergence: what it is, how it's computed, and where it shows up in LLMs and PPO training.">

<div id="read-progress"></div>

<div class="blog-shell">
  <div class="nav-column">
    <nav id="section-nav" aria-label="Section navigation">
      <div class="section-index-label mono">Index</div>
      <ul class="section-index" id="sectionIndex"></ul>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <article class="blog-post">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section" id="s0" data-label="Intro">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-tag mono">10 min read · ML Fundamentals</div>
      <h1>KL Divergence<br><em>made visual</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">No scary math. Just two distributions,<br>and how far apart they are.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Section 1 — Distribution -->
  <section class="section" id="s1" data-label="Distributions">
    <div class="section-label mono">01 — The Big Idea</div>
    <h2>What even is a distribution?</h2>
    <p>Before KL Loss, let's get comfortable with distributions. A <strong>probability distribution</strong> tells you how likely each outcome is. Think of it as a "belief" about what will happen.</p>
    <p>Below are two distributions — <strong>P</strong> (the true one) and <strong>Q</strong> (our guess). Drag the sliders and watch them shift.</p>

    <div class="canvas-wrap">
      <canvas id="distCanvas" height="155"></canvas>
      <div class="controls">
        <span class="ctrl-label mono">P peak position</span>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="100" value="35" id="pPeak" step="1">
        <span class="ctrl-val mono" id="pPeakVal">35%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="controls">
        <span class="ctrl-label mono">Q peak position</span>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="100" value="65" id="qPeak" step="1">
        <span class="ctrl-val mono" id="qPeakVal">65%</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>When P and Q overlap perfectly, they're identical. When they drift apart — that gap is exactly what KL divergence measures.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2 — Formula -->
  <section class="section" id="s2" data-label="The Formula">
    <div class="section-label mono">02 — The Formula</div>
    <h2>What KL divergence actually measures</h2>
    <p>KL divergence answers: <strong>"How much extra information do I waste if I use Q to describe a world that's actually P?"</strong></p>

    <div class="formula-box">
      <div class="formula mono">KL(P ∥ Q) = Σ P(x) · log( P(x) / Q(x) )</div>
      <div class="formula-sub">Sum over all outcomes x. P is truth, Q is our approximation.</div>
    </div>

    <p>Three things to notice:</p>
    <div class="props-list">
      <div class="prop-item">
        <span class="prop-num mono">1.</span>
        <span>It's <strong>not symmetric</strong> — KL(P∥Q) ≠ KL(Q∥P). Direction matters.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prop-item">
        <span class="prop-num mono">2.</span>
        <span>It's always <strong>≥ 0</strong>. Zero means the distributions are identical.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prop-item">
        <span class="prop-num mono">3.</span>
        <span>The <strong>log ratio</strong> captures surprise — when Q says something is rare but P says it's common, that's expensive.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3 — Live Calculation -->
  <section class="section" id="s3" data-label="Live Calc">
    <div class="section-label mono">03 — Live Calculation</div>
    <h2>Let's compute it ourselves</h2>
    <p>Three outcomes: Rain, Sunny, and Cloudy. P is the actual weather, Q is the forecast.</p>

    <div class="calc-panel">
      <div class="calc-panel-header">
        <span class="calc-panel-title mono">KL(P ∥ Q)</span>
        <div class="calc-kl-pill mono">
          <span class="calc-kl-val" id="klResult">—</span>
          <span class="calc-kl-unit">nats</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="calc-sliders">
        <div class="calc-slider-card">
          <label class="calc-slider-label mono" for="p0">Rain · P (truth)</label>
          <div class="calc-slider-row">
            <input type="range" min="5" max="85" value="50" id="p0" step="5">
            <span class="calc-slider-val mono" id="p0val">50%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-slider-card">
          <label class="calc-slider-label mono" for="q0">Rain · Q (forecast)</label>
          <div class="calc-slider-row">
            <input type="range" min="5" max="85" value="20" id="q0" step="5">
            <span class="calc-slider-val mono" id="q0val">20%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-slider-card">
          <label class="calc-slider-label mono" for="split">Sunny share of remainder</label>
          <div class="calc-slider-row">
            <input type="range" min="10" max="80" value="50" id="split" step="5">
            <span class="calc-slider-val mono" id="splitval">50%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="calc-outcomes" id="klBreakdown"></div>

      <p class="calc-note">As P and Q align, KL approaches <strong>0</strong>. The farther apart they are, the higher the penalty.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4 — LLMs / PPO -->
  <section class="section" id="s4" data-label="KL in LLMs">
    <div class="section-label mono">04 — In the Wild: LLMs</div>
    <h2>Where does this show up in AI?</h2>
    <p>When training a language model with <strong>PPO (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback)</strong>, we want the new model to improve — but not drift too far from the original. KL divergence is the leash.</p>

    <div class="ppo-box">
      <div class="ppo-models">
        <div class="model-card">
          <div class="model-name">Parent model</div>
          <div class="model-sub">Original pretrained LLM<br>Distribution = P</div>
        </div>
        <div class="arrow-mid mono">fine-tune</div>
        <div class="model-card">
          <div class="model-name">Student model</div>
          <div class="model-sub">Fine-tuned version<br>Distribution = Q</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ppo-formula mono">
        PPO loss = reward signal <span class="accent">− β · KL(Q ∥ P)</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ppo-note">The KL term punishes the student for straying too far from the parent.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Section 5 — Token by Token -->
  <section class="section" id="s5" data-label="Token by Token">
    <div class="section-label mono">05 — Token by Token</div>
    <h2>A real example: "What is the capital of France?"</h2>
    <p>The student replies: <em>"The capital of France is Paris"</em>. Each token gets its own probability from both models. Click a token to see how the distributions compare.</p>

    <div class="token-layout">
      <div class="token-col-main">
        <div class="token-scene">
          <div class="sentence-box" id="tokenSentence"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout callout-tight">
          <p>In practice, we only measure KL loss on the <strong>tokens the student actually generates</strong> — not the entire vocabulary. This is the "sample KL" approximation used in real training pipelines.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="token-col-detail" id="tokenDetail">
        <p class="token-placeholder" id="tokenPlaceholder">Click a token to compare parent vs student distributions.</p>
        <div class="token-detail-body" id="tokenDetailBody" hidden>
          <div class="token-detail-header">
            <span class="token-badge mono" id="tokenTitle"></span>
            <div class="token-kl-pill mono">
              <span class="token-kl-val" id="tokenKL">—</span>
              <span class="token-kl-unit">nats</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p id="tokenDesc" class="token-desc"></p>
          <div class="token-compare">
            <div class="token-model-block">
              <div class="token-model-label">
                <span class="dot" style="background:#7F77DD"></span> Parent model (P)
              </div>
              <div class="token-bar-list" id="parentBars"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="token-model-block">
              <div class="token-model-label">
                <span class="dot" style="background:#1D9E75"></span> Student model (Q)
              </div>
              <div class="token-bar-list" id="studentBars"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Section 6 — Forward vs Reverse -->
  <section class="section" id="s6" data-label="Forward vs Reverse">
    <div class="section-label mono">06 — Forward vs Reverse</div>
    <h2>KL(P∥Q) vs KL(Q∥P) — does direction matter?</h2>
    <p>Yes — a lot. They measure different things and lead to different model behaviors.</p>

    <div class="reverse-compare">
      <div class="rev-card forward">
        <h4>Forward KL(P ∥ Q)</h4>
        <p>Penalizes Q for putting low probability where P puts high probability. Q tries to <strong>cover all modes</strong> of P — even if it spreads too thin.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rev-card reverse">
        <h4>Reverse KL(Q ∥ P)</h4>
        <p>Penalizes Q for putting high probability where P puts low probability. Q <strong>picks one mode and sharpens</strong> onto it — mode-seeking behavior.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:1rem">The <strong>On-Policy Self-Distillation</strong> method uses reverse KL. The student model generates outputs, then is trained to match its own good generations — making it sharper and more confident.</p>

    <div class="canvas-wrap">
      <canvas id="reverseCanvas" height="155"></canvas>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:0.75rem; margin-top:0.75rem; flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button type="button" class="play-btn" data-kl-mode="forward">Forward KL</button>
        <button type="button" class="play-btn" data-kl-mode="reverse">Reverse KL</button>
      </div>
      <div id="klModeExplain" class="kl-mode-explain"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 7 — Recap -->
  <section class="section" id="s7" data-label="Recap">
    <div class="section-label mono">Recap</div>
    <h2>The 30-second summary</h2>
    <div class="recap-list">
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>KL divergence</strong> measures how different distribution Q is from distribution P.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>KL(P∥Q) = Σ P(x) · log(P/Q)</strong> — always non-negative, zero when identical.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>In LLMs (PPO)</strong>, it keeps the student model from drifting too far from the parent.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>Reverse KL</strong> is used in self-distillation for sharper, mode-seeking behavior.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  </article>
</div>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Full-screen scroll snap ── */
  :global(html) {
    scroll-snap-type: y mandatory;
    scroll-padding-top: 50px;
  }
  :global(body > .page-shell > footer) {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ── Progress bar ── */
  #read-progress {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    height: 2px;
    width: 0%;
    background: #7F77DD;
    z-index: 9999;
    transition: width 0.1s linear;
  }

  /* ── Shell: nav column + content column (no overlap) ── */
  .blog-shell {
    --content-width: 56rem;
    --nav-width: 7.5rem;
    --shell-gap: 2rem;
    --shell-width: min(calc(var(--content-width) + var(--nav-width) + var(--shell-gap)), calc(100vw - 3rem));
    width: var(--shell-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--nav-width) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--shell-gap);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .nav-column {
    width: var(--nav-width);
    min-height: 1px;
    position: relative;
  }

  /* ── Section index (left; active centered, others faded) ── */
  #section-nav {
    position: fixed;
    top: 50%;
    left: 1.75rem;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    z-index: 100;
    width: max-content;
    max-width: 11rem;
    overflow: visible;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .section-index-label {
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    padding-left: 0.1rem;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .section-index {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }
  :global(.section-index-item) {
    display: block;
    width: max-content;
    max-width: 11rem;
    text-align: left;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    padding: 7px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--text-3);
    opacity: 0.5;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease, color 0.35s ease;
  }
  :global(.section-index-item:hover) {
    opacity: 0.72;
  }
  :global(.section-index-item.active) {
    opacity: 1;
    color: #534AB7;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"] .section-index-item.active) {
    color: #9B93F0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .blog-shell {
      --content-width: min(56rem, calc(100vw - 3rem));
      --shell-width: var(--content-width);
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .nav-column,
    #section-nav { display: none; }
  }

  /* ── Layout ── */
  .blog-post {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 0; }
  .hero-tag {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .hero h1 em {
    font-family: "Lora", serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #7F77DD;
  }
  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ── Sections (one viewport below nav; content centered, no inner scroll) ── */
  .section {
    --section-h: calc(100vh - 50px);
    --section-h: calc(100dvh - 50px);
    height: var(--section-h);
    min-height: var(--section-h);
    max-height: var(--section-h);
    overflow: hidden;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
    scroll-snap-stop: always;
    scroll-margin-top: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    justify-content: safe center;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .section > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .section h2 { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  .section p { margin-bottom: 0.55rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .section .callout { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  .section .canvas-wrap { margin: 0.65rem 0; padding: 0.75rem; }
  .section .formula-box { margin: 0.65rem 0; padding: 1rem; }
  .section .props-list { margin: 0.45rem 0; gap: 0.45rem; }
  .section .ppo-box { margin: 0.65rem 0; padding: 1rem; }
  .section .controls { margin: 0.35rem 0; }
  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  p strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  p em { font-family: "Lora", serif; font-style: italic; }

  .divider {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ── Callout ── */
  .callout {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-left: 3px solid #7F77DD;
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }
  .callout p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .callout-tight {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    margin: 0.45rem 0 !important;
  }
  .callout-tight p { font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  /* ── Live calc panel ── */
  .calc-panel {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }
  .calc-panel-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.65rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .calc-panel-title {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  .calc-kl-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: #EEEDFE;
    border: 1px solid #AFA9EC;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .calc-kl-pill {
    background: #1d1c35;
    border-color: #3d3870;
  }
  .calc-kl-val {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #534AB7;
  }
  .calc-kl-unit {
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .calc-kl-val { color: #9B93F0; }
  .calc-sliders {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .calc-slider-card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
  }
  .calc-slider-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .calc-slider-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .calc-slider-row input[type=range] {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    accent-color: #7F77DD;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .calc-slider-val {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 2.25rem;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .calc-outcomes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }
  :global(.calc-outcome) {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  :global(.calc-outcome-name) {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  :global(.calc-outcome-contrib) {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: #534AB7;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"] .calc-outcome-contrib) { color: #9B93F0; }
  :global(.calc-outcome-head) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  :global(.calc-prob-row) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1rem 1fr 2.25rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  :global(.calc-prob-label) {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #534AB7;
  }
  :global(.calc-prob-label.is-q) { color: #1D9E75; }
  :global(.calc-prob-pct) {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  :global(.calc-math) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  }
  :global(.calc-math span:last-child) {
    color: #534AB7;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"] .calc-math span:last-child) { color: #9B93F0; }
  .calc-note {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
  }
  .calc-note strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .calc-sliders,
    .calc-outcomes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* ── Token side-by-side ── */
  .token-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .token-scene { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; }
  .token-col-detail {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    min-height: 14rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .token-col-detail.is-populated {
    justify-content: flex-start;
  }
  .token-placeholder {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .token-detail-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .token-detail-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .token-badge {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 5px 11px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: #EEEDFE;
    color: #534AB7;
    border: 1px solid #AFA9EC;
  }
